 "tag_notes": {
  "P slot+rule": "DRAFT: slots plus its placement rule (SPACE 4.1).",
  "C self": "Each group's leader heals its own replicas (CELL, V4). No slot moves.",
  "C self+p": "self plus an optional planner whose hints name the config they read (the draft).",
  "C self+mv": "COMP: each group's leader heals its own replicas; one loop on #meta's leader only proposes slot moves (AMENDMENTS 4, footnotes 14 and 15).",
  "C cent(writers)": "SLOG footnote 5: the writer changes its log nodes; the controller changes writers.",
  "C cent(manifest CAS)": "OBJ footnote 7: CAS on the object store's manifest.",
  "Q mix": "maj-d by default, maj-m and none per resource (AMENDMENTS 2, Q).",
  "Q maj-d(log nodes)": "SLOG footnote 6: a write quorum of the log nodes.",
  "S jrnl +tier(store)": "Footnote 1: an object store is required across boxes (draft decision 23a).",
  "K lib(srv) / F all(srv)": "SRV footnote 2: the server folds plain rows in Rust; data's views run on clients and relays.",
  "V +lrn(standby)": "LEAN footnote 3: one warm standby that folds.",
  "I port(meta)": "Footnote 4: Raft for the metadata group only.",
  "V tier +lrn(servers fold) / F all(servers)": "RLOG footnote 9: log members vote; servers are full learners that fold; the writer is a server holding a writer epoch.",
  "F all(isolates)": "EMB-V8 footnote 10: data folds inside V8 isolates in the server.",
  "F ldr(app folds)": "SIDE footnote 11: the app's Node process folds for the groups its host leads; every app folds what it follows.",
  "Y fwd(local daemon)": "SIDE: writes go to the local daemon, which forwards.",
  "Z par": "No judged row holds it. E-37 modelled it; AMENDMENTS 4 proposes COMP+par.",
  "S lsm +tier": "No judged row holds it. An LSM store (PD's) with old data and snapshots also sent to an object store, as the review's PD+fix (TiKV's shape with fixes) needs. SPACE 2 S lists +tier as a modifier of a log store."
 },
 "search_options": "The closure search uses, on each axis, the tags some judged row holds, minus BUY's outside/theirs tags, plus two tags no judged row holds but the review priced: Z par (E-37) and S lsm +tier (PD+fix)."
}